-- V50: Imports the full CareerGuide Career Taxonomy (see uploaded
-- 'CareerGuide -- Discipline, Specialization & Job Role Taxonomy' PDF)
-- as the taxonomy-first pass agreed with the user: complete, correctly
-- linked structure across all 11 Career Domains / 42 Disciplines / ~250
-- Specializations / ~300 Job Roles, with LIGHTWEIGHT PLACEHOLDER content
-- for every field the source document doesn't supply (it gives names
-- and hierarchy only -- no tagline/salary/education/description/etc for
-- any entity). Rich, hand-written content is a deliberate follow-up pass
-- per domain, not attempted here.
--
-- Mapping onto the existing schema (matches the PDF's own section 15/17
-- architecture almost exactly): Career Domain -> existing `categories`
-- (10 of 11 domains already existed; only mapped, none created here),
-- Discipline -> `careers`, Specialization -> `specializations`,
-- Job Role -> `job_roles`. Specializations and Job Roles that repeat
-- verbatim across multiple disciplines in the source (e.g. "Cloud
-- Computing" under both Computer Science & Engineering and Information
-- Technology; "Manufacturing Engineer" under three disciplines) are
-- deduplicated into one row each and linked to every discipline that
-- names them, per the PDF's own section 14.1/14.3 modeling principle
-- ("a specialization can be related to multiple disciplines").
--
-- Deliberately NOT attempted here: specialization_job_roles (granular
-- specialization -> job-role links). The source only gives one such
-- example (section 14.2, Software Engineering) and otherwise lists
-- Specializations and Job Roles as flat sibling lists per discipline --
-- mapping every job role to a specific specialization across ~250
-- specializations and ~300 job roles would mean fabricating ~250
-- judgment calls the source doesn't support. Job roles ARE linked at
-- the discipline level via career_job_roles (the same relation the
-- existing Software Engineer career already used, from V26).

-- 42 disciplines, 265 distinct specializations, 247 distinct job roles.
-- 270 discipline<->specialization links, 265 discipline<->job-role links.





